    analysis: benchmark floors, FineTasks criteria, language panel; docs
    
    Three new analyses from the review of what the older experiments, the
    public models, FineTasks and language transfer can still add
    (plan/next_analyses.md), each in its RQ's driver block, CSV beside every PNG,
    README auto block, check_rules 0 findings:
    
    - rq00 benchmark_floor.py: the ladder's per-task gate floor against the
      public models' (all/external mask). Of the 35 old-list tasks the ladder
      never reads, public models read 25 at <= 1.7B (size/recipe floor), 5 at
      7-14B, 2 at >= 27B, 3 never (benchmark or language floor).
    - rq09 finetasks_criteria.py: FineTasks' four selection criteria computed
      per (task, size) on the 18 design variants and judged by DA-size against
      1.7B. Passers 0.55-0.56 vs failers 0.45-0.49; their SNR > 20 does not
      discriminate; every letter-format pick of theirs passes only as its rf_
      twin. finetasks_overlap.csv maps their 96 picks to our registry.
    - rq06 language_panel.py: one language / English / the panel macro at the
      proxy against the 1.7B macro ranking over the L8 panel. English alone is
      the worst single-language proxy (0.59 at 1B vs 0.65-0.71); the panel
      macro reaches 0.81-0.93 on hellaswag, Global-MMLU-rf, LAMBADA, INCLUDE-rfgm.
    
    CLAUDE.md: the two periods (36-sweep vs ladder) and why they are never
    pooled; pointer to the rq00-rq02 analysis README. signal-and-noise CLAUDE.md:
    pipeline in RQ order, one-figure regeneration recipe with the thread caps,
    the three rq02 facts every reading must respect, predictivity_schemes note,
    bug-history entries 16 (figure drawn before its input) and 17 (filtering on
    the quantity drawn).
    
    Also carries the analysis tables and README blocks regenerated by the
    2026-09-23 refresh.

